BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exposure Trip : a triple Reportback from the Philippines
UID:evenement9020 @ http://www.resistancemontreal.org
DTSTAMP:20260718T124504Z
DTSTART:20260728T210000Z
DTEND:20260728T144200Z
CREATED:20260718T124504Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260718T124504Z 
LOCATION:Au Monastère, 4450 St-Hubert (métro Mont-Royal) 
DESCRIPTION:Earlier this year\, members of the Montreal-based Anakbayan chapter spent a month in the Philippines living alongside our people. Through this exposure trip\, we witnessed firsthand the semi-feudal and semi-colonial conditions of the Philippine society that continue to force thousands of Filipinos to leave the country every day in search of jobs abroad\, like here in Canada. Join us as we share our experiences\, reflections\, and lessons from the communities we immersed in\, and discuss what these realities mean for the struggle of the Filipino people—both in the Philippines and in the diaspora. ⏰ July 28\, Tuesday from 5–8 PM 📍Au monastère (4450 rue Saint-Hubert\, room 600) ♿ wheelchair accessible entrace 4449\, rue Berri Near Metro Mont-Royal Free event ! hybrid TBD
CATEGORIES:événements
URL:https://www.resistancemontreal.org/calendrier/article/evenements?id_evenement=9020

STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
