BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celebrating Independance\, Remembering Partition : Screening of Ajay Bhardwaj’s PUNJAB TRILOGY in the presence of the filmmaker
UID:evenement9078 @ http://www.resistancemontreal.org
DTSTAMP:20260809T145527Z
DTSTART:20260823T160000Z
DTEND:20260823T165200Z
CREATED:20260809T145527Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T145527Z 
LOCATION:SAWCC, South Asian Women's Community Center\, 1035 Rachel est\, 3rd floor (métro Mont-Royal) 
DESCRIPTION:CELEBRATING INDEPENDENCE\, REMEMBERING PARTITION Screening of Ajay Bhardwaj’s PUNJAB TRILOGY in the presence of the filmmaker Sunday 23rd August\, 12 noon to 6 pm At SAWCC (South Asian Women’s Community Centre) 1035 Rachel est 3rd floor (metro Mont Royal) With Food and Snacks ! “Close to a million people lost their lives and several million lost their homelands forever when India and Pakistan were partitioned. In the midst of the horror that Hindus\, Muslims\, and Sikhs inflicted on each other there were also redeeming stories of the love that bound these communities together—stories we cling to\, so we may retain our faith in the human spirit. 'Milange Babey Ratan De Mele Te' is one such story. It is the story of how love survived a holocaust.” — Arundhati Roy There will be short breaks between the screening of each film of the trilogy for conversation and refreshments and a discussion with the filmmaker at the end. Program : ======= ★ 12:30pm - Kitte Mil Ve Mahi (Where the Twain Shall Meet) 70'/2005 A film which explores the bond between Dalits and Sufism\, which is both healing and emancipatory. ★ 2pm - Rabba Hun Kee Kariye (Thus Departed Our Neighbours) 65'/2007 The film engages for the first time with feelings of guilt and remorse about the genocidal violence in Punjab's countryside. ★ 3:30pm - Milange Babey Ratan De Mele Te (Let's Meet at Baba Ratan's Fair) 95'/2012 A film excavating local cultural continuities and a most imaginative transgression of religious identities in post-partition Punjab. ★ 5pm - Q&A with the filmmaker\, Ajay Bhardwaj Discussant : Prof. Pasha M. Khan All are welcome ! Organized by CERAS (South Asia Centre\, a forum) Supported by SADAC (South Asia Diaspora Action Collective) @sadacmtl & Rang Collective @rangcollective
CATEGORIES:événements
URL:https://www.resistancemontreal.org/calendrier/article/evenements?id_evenement=9078

STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
